      "new_sha256": "62aab1fe8eea9cfaab4dad10bfafc16ffba2d51d2a808691e628a42f1b445969",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-12560",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $\\boldsymbol x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} - \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis, and $b=2, \\: c=\\dfrac 12.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-12560.json",
          "file_sha256": "fd1808a8660edab4831a6b5598b0851e1000acd26b4c0d59db5a45fe04fb7f5d"
